  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_036 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.715 acc, a substantial jump over the best RNA-only (0.650), confirming that the image modality adds meaningful signal. However, we have only tested one fusion strategy (concat) in the multimodal setting. Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation when combining a strong RNA encoder (scvi_n200) with a strong image encoder (imagenet_vit_l)? Given that the two modalities have very different standalone performance (RNA ~0.65 vs image ~0.21), a weighted fusion that down-weights the weaker modality could improve the joint representation. Why this is the best next experiment: config_037 is a minimal, single-variable change from the current best (only fusion: concat→weighted), giving a clean A/B comparison that directly reduces uncertainty about whether the fusion mechanism is a bottleneck. The result will inform whether to invest further in fusion tuning or to pivot toward other dimensions (e.g., aggregation strategy or image encoder choice) in subsequent experiments."
}

